---
title: Schools Reinventing Counties
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block head %}
<style>
  /* ── PAGE HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .prog-hero {
    background: var(--navy); background-image: var(--grid-navy);
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 55% 45%;
    padding-top: 64px; align-items: end;
  }
  .prog-hero-content {
    padding: 100px 72px 80px 80px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center;
  }
  .prog-hero-visual { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; }
  .prog-hero-visual img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .prog-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .prog-hero-content { padding: 80px 32px 60px; }
    .prog-hero-visual { display: none; }
  }
  .prog-hero-eyebrow {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: rgba(139,163,194,0.5);
    text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .prog-hero-h1 {
    font-family: 'Big Shoulders Display', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(56px, 6.5vw, 96px);
    line-height: 0.91; color: var(--cream); letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .prog-hero-sub {
    font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--civic);
    max-width: 560px; margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .prog-hero-cta { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  /* ── OVERVIEW ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .overview-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; margin-top: 48px; }
  .overview-body { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .overview-cards-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .overview-card {
    border: 1.5px solid var(--soft); padding: 20px 24px;
    font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--gray);
  }

  /* ── DESIGN PROCESS ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .process-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
  .pillar-sm { padding: 32px 28px; }
  .pillar-sm .pillar-num { font-size: 48px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .pillar-sm .pillar-title { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .pillar-sm .pillar-body { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }

  /* ── THREE PILLARS ON CREAM ─────────────────────────────────── */
  .pillars-cream { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 48px; }
  .pillar-card-lbl {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--red); margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .pillar-card-title {
    font-family: 'Big Shoulders Display', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: 26px; color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.05; margin-bottom: 16px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  /* ── THE WORLD BUILD ────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .world-header { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .world-header-body { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--civic); }
  .world-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr; gap: 80px; align-items: center; }
  .world-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    background: rgba(22,43,77,0.5);
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(22,43,77,0.8);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  }
  .world-placeholder-lbl {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: rgba(139,163,194,0.55); text-align: center;
    text-transform: uppercase; line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .world-lbl {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(139,163,194,0.5); margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .world-lbl + .card-list { margin-bottom: 36px; }
  .world-card-list li { color: var(--civic); }
  .world-card-list li::before { background: var(--red); }

  /* ── QUOTE BAND ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .quote-band {
    border-top: 4px solid var(--red);
    background: var(--cream); padding: 80px 80px;
  }
  .quote-text {
    font-family: 'Big Shoulders Display', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 44px);
    color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 840px; margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .quote-attr { font-size: 14px; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.6; }
  .quote-attr strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ── WHY IT WORKS ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .stakes-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; margin-top: 48px; }
  .stakes-body { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .stakes-cards { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .stakes-card { border: 1.5px solid var(--soft); padding: 20px 24px; }
  .stakes-card-lbl {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--red); margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .stakes-card-text { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--gray); }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<!-- HERO -->
<div class="prog-hero">
  <div class="prog-hero-content">
    <div class="prog-hero-eyebrow">The Program</div>
    <h1 class="prog-hero-h1">Schools Reinventing Counties.</h1>
    <p class="prog-hero-sub">
      A statewide community design program built in Minecraft Education. Students explore their county, investigate a real local challenge, design a solution, and pitch it to the leaders who can act on it.
    </p>
    <div class="prog-hero-cta">
      <a href="/submit/" class="btn-cream">Get Your School Involved</a>
      <a href="#" class="btn-ghost-civic">Download the Field Guide →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="prog-hero-visual">
    <img src="/assets/kids-collage.png" alt="Students collaborating on a civic design project">
  </div>
</div>

<!-- OVERVIEW -->
<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2">The program that turns<br>civics into action.</h2>
  <div class="overview-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="overview-body">Schools Reinventing Counties connects classroom learning to authentic community challenges. Students don't just learn about local government — they investigate a real problem, build a solution, and pitch it to the people in charge.</p>
      <p class="overview-body">The program is built on one principle: a real location, a specific problem, and a real audience produce deeper student work than an open-ended prompt. When students know their ideas can reach the people actually making decisions, they stop playing and start advocating.</p>
      <p class="overview-body">Students enter an immersive Minecraft world modeled on their county. They meet community members, gather evidence, and investigate a real local challenge — housing, transportation, sustainability, or public space. Then they design and build a solution, record a 3-minute walkthrough, and enter the Battle of the Counties.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="overview-cards-col">
      <div class="overview-card">A Minecraft world built around your students' actual county — not a generic environment</div>
      <div class="overview-card">A real community challenge, not a fictional scenario</div>
      <div class="overview-card">A live pitch to local leaders who are present to listen — not just to evaluate</div>
      <div class="overview-card">Standards-aligned across multiple subject areas</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- DESIGN PROCESS -->
<section class="sec sec-navy">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-light page-h2" style="margin-bottom: 32px;">Eight steps.<br>One community.</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--civic); max-width: 560px; margin-bottom: 56px;">
    Every experience follows the same design process, regardless of which county students explore. Understanding always comes before designing.
  </p>
  <div class="process-grid">
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">01</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Explore</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Observe the community. Notice landmarks, public spaces, and natural features before attempting to improve anything.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">02</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Listen</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Meet Community Guides, local leaders, historians, and subject matter experts. Every conversation offers a different perspective.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">03</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Investigate</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Ask questions. Collect information. Discover how history, geography, culture, and economics shape a community.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">04</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Understand</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Connect what you've learned. Identify patterns, opportunities, and problems still waiting for a thoughtful solution.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">05</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Imagine</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Brainstorm possibilities. Explore multiple ideas before choosing one. Innovation begins with curiosity, not certainty.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">06</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Design</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Create a solution that responds to what you've learned. Every design decision should reflect authentic community needs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">07</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Build</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Bring your idea to life in Minecraft Education. Every block should have a purpose — the build is the argument made visible.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">08</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Share</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Record a 3-minute walkthrough. Explain your thinking, your evidence, and your design. Then enter the Battle of the Counties.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- THREE PILLARS (expanded on cream) -->
<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2" style="margin-bottom: 32px;">Three pillars.<br>One program.</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--gray); max-width: 640px;">
    Schools Reinventing Counties is built at the intersection of three disciplines that rarely share a classroom. Together, they produce something no single subject area can on its own.
  </p>
  <div class="pillars-cream">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="pillar-card-lbl">Pillar 01</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-card-title">STEM & Digital Literacy</h3>
      <p class="card-body" style="margin-bottom: 20px;">Spatial reasoning, coding logic, and engineering design in a native digital environment. Students think like engineers while building real solutions.</p>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>Spatial reasoning and architectural thinking</li>
        <li>Coding logic and computational design</li>
        <li>Engineering design principles</li>
        <li>Digital citizenship and responsible technology use</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="pillar-card-lbl">Pillar 02</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-card-title">Civic Engagement</h3>
      <p class="card-body" style="margin-bottom: 20px;">Systems thinking, community problem-solving, and public policy exploration through authentic local challenges and real decision-makers.</p>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>Systems thinking and policy analysis</li>
        <li>Community investigation and evidence gathering</li>
        <li>Stakeholder perspective-taking and empathy</li>
        <li>High-stakes civic communication</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="pillar-card-lbl">Pillar 03</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-card-title">Academic Esports</h3>
      <p class="card-body" style="margin-bottom: 20px;">Real-time collaboration, consensus-building, and high-stakes presentation skills — in a competitive format that students actually want to win.</p>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>Team strategy and real-time collaboration</li>
        <li>Consensus-building under competitive pressure</li>
        <li>Public presentation and high-stakes communication</li>
        <li>Resilience and performance under real stakes</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- THE WORLD BUILD -->
<section class="sec sec-navy">
  <div class="world-header">
    <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-light page-h2">Built for your county.</h2>
    <p class="world-header-body">Every participating county gets a custom Minecraft Education world — grounded in real local geography, landmarks, and community life. Your staff builds nothing. The world comes ready to explore.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="world-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="world-placeholder">
        <div class="world-placeholder-lbl">Image placeholder<br>Minecraft county world</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="world-lbl">What's inside every world</div>
      <ul class="card-list world-card-list" style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
        <li>A Community Hub where students begin and select their challenge area</li>
        <li>County-specific landmarks, neighborhoods, natural features, and civic spaces</li>
        <li>NPCs representing real community voices: guides, local leaders, historians, scientists, and subject matter experts</li>
        <li>A Community Design Mentor who presents the Design Challenge</li>
        <li>A designated build zone where students construct their solution</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="world-lbl">How the world is made</div>
      <ul class="card-list world-card-list">
        <li>Built by Lifeboat Studios — no work required from school staff or teachers</li>
        <li>Grounded in real county geography, history, and community priorities</li>
        <li>Runs on Minecraft Education, accessible through school or district licensing</li>
        <li>Designed for multiple class sessions — not meant to be completed in one sitting</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- QUOTE -->
<div class="quote-band">
  <p class="quote-text">"This is not about playing a game. It is about student voice, civic engagement, and showing our students that their ideas can lead real change."</p>
  <div class="quote-attr"><strong>Dr. Stefan Bean</strong>, Orange County Superintendent of Schools</div>
</div>

<!-- WHY IT WORKS -->
<section class="sec sec-cream" style="padding-top: 80px;">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2" style="margin-bottom: 48px;">Why this model works.</h2>
  <div class="stakes-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="stakes-body">A real location, a specific problem, and a real audience produce deeper student work than an open-ended prompt. That's the core insight the program is built on.</p>
      <p class="stakes-body">Students who know their ideas can reach the people actually making decisions don't treat the work as schoolwork. They treat it as a platform. The build gets more detailed. The research gets more thorough. The pitch gets rehearsed.</p>
      <p class="stakes-body">This model has a track record. NYC students redesigned the Kingsbridge Armory and presented at City Hall. Jacksonville students' builds reached the urban planners actively redesigning the site. Calgary students moved from in-game advocacy to in-person advocacy for an accessible entertainment district.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="stakes-cards">
        <div class="stakes-card">
          <div class="stakes-card-lbl">Place</div>
          <p class="stakes-card-text">Their county, their community, their neighbors — not a fictional scenario</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stakes-card">
          <div class="stakes-card-lbl">Problem</div>
          <p class="stakes-card-text">Housing, transportation, sustainability, public space — real challenges with no easy answer</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stakes-card">
          <div class="stakes-card-lbl">Audience</div>
          <p class="stakes-card-text">Local leaders who are present to listen, not just to evaluate</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="/#competition" class="btn-primary">See the Battle of the Counties →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA BAND -->
<div class="cta-band">
  <div class="cta-band-inner">
    <h2 class="cta-band-h2">Ready to bring this<br>to your students?</h2>
    <p class="cta-band-body">
      Schools in participating counties can register now. The worlds come built, training is provided, and the competition is structured. You bring the students.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-band-btns">
      <a href="/educators/" class="btn-white">For Educators</a>
      <a href="/submit/" class="btn-white">Submit a Project</a>
      <a href="/partners/" class="btn-ghost-white">Partner with us →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% endblock %}
